Third-party software
--------------------

Byori Studio is built with, and its application bundle contains compiled code
from, open source libraries. Each remains under its own license; the full
dependency lists with exact versions are package-lock.json and
src-tauri/Cargo.lock. Direct dependencies:

  Desktop shell and service (Rust)
    Tauri, tauri-build                MIT OR Apache-2.0
    Tokio, Axum, Tower, tower-http    MIT
    Serde, serde_json                 MIT OR Apache-2.0
    reqwest                           MIT OR Apache-2.0
    futures-util, uuid, semver, sha2  MIT OR Apache-2.0
    tracing, tracing-subscriber       MIT
    rfd, plist                        MIT
    dirs                              MIT OR Apache-2.0
    image                             MIT OR Apache-2.0
    fontdue                           MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR Zlib

  User interface (JavaScript)
    React, React DOM                  MIT
    @tauri-apps/api                   MIT OR Apache-2.0
    lucide-react (Lucide icons)       ISC

External programs
-----------------

Byori Studio does not include the following programs. It runs the copies
installed on the user's computer, under their own licenses:

  FFmpeg and ffprobe (media probing, preview frames, proxies, rendering)
  Python 3 (the local MCP bridge in scripts/)
  OpenAI Whisper (optional automatic captions)
  macOS "say" (system text-to-speech)
  Claude Code, Codex CLI and Gemini CLI (optional editing agents)
  Node.js with the mcp-remote package (optional Higgsfield connection)
  ByoriDB (optional creative memory database)

Demonstration media
-------------------

The files in public/demo are bundled only for the explicitly labelled example
project. Their origin is recorded in public/demo/SOURCES.md:

  coast.jpg, mountain.jpg, lake.jpg
    Photographs downloaded from Unsplash (images.unsplash.com; the exact URLs
    are listed in SOURCES.md) and used under the Unsplash License,
    https://unsplash.com/license.
  ambient.wav
    Synthesized locally with FFmpeg's sine source. It contains no recorded
    music or third-party material.
